## Crates

One row per crate, grouped by the licence elected for it and sorted by name
within each group. `cargo-about` records each crate's own licence text
separately — the copyright lines differ — so the full texts live on the site
rather than here.

That is also why this table is post-processed. `cargo-about` emits one row per
licence *text*, grouping crates by which text they share, and a crate that
ships several files scanning as the same licence has its text chosen by the
order those files are read off disk. Group membership, and so each row's
position, then varies from machine to machine. `scripts/attribution.sh` sorts
the rows, collapses the duplicates a crate with several notices produces, and
recomputes the counts above from what is left, which is what makes this file
reproducible. The elected licence ids are unaffected either way.

